## Summary

**What was failing:**
1. Stdin tests were always prefixing output with `(standard input)` even without `-H`
2. Single file tests were not matching because `first_operand_index` was being overwritten on each non-option argument, causing pattern_index to point to the wrong argument

**Changes made to `/Users/sonjabrown/agentic_cyber/runs/formal/grep-qwen3-topk40-t0-p1-seed42-maxtok32768-loops1-n10/lineage-001/001/temp-0p0/attempt-001/workdir/src/new_grep/new_grep.c`:**

1. Line 150: Changed `first_operand_index = 1` to `first_operand_index = -1`
2. Line 166: Changed condition from `if (first_operand_index == 1)` to `if (first_operand_index < 0)`
3. Line 171: Changed `pattern_index = first_operand_index > 0 ? ...` to `pattern_index = first_operand_index >= 0 ? ...`
4. Lines 175-178: Fixed file argument count logic and prefix decision
5. Lines 182-196: Stdin now respects `-H` flag for prefixing

**Build command:** `mkdir -p build && cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic -O2 src/new_grep/new_grep.c -o build/new_grep`

**All 60 tests pass (51 base + 9 with_filename).**
